# decision Pub uses the native nested Git descriptor

The Pub adapter owns one two-space-indented entry under top-level `dependencies`. It writes
`git.url`, the full `LockedDependency.Commit` as `git.ref`, and optional `git.path`; requested
branch names are never written. It splices only that YAML entry, preserving every unrelated byte.
Inline dependency maps are rejected as not wirable instead of being reformatted.
If top-level `dependencies` is absent, the adapter creates a delimited mapping and removes the
container as a unit on unwire.

# decision Pub lifecycle materializes packages

`Pull` runs `dart pub get`, including when the declaration is unchanged, to refresh
`pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/package_config.json`. `Remove` deletes only the owned root
declaration and runs the same Pub convergence, retaining unrelated and transitively required
packages.

# test Pub adapter

- Fixture/golden wiring is idempotent and preserves comments and unrelated dependencies.
- A subdirectory export writes `git.path`; drift checks URL and locked ref.
- Unwire restores the original fixture bytes.

# decision Pub lifecycle prerequisite

`Pull` and `Remove` check `dart` through the shared prerequisite contract before invoking
`dart pub get`. `Inspect` is offline and checks the exact `resolved-ref` in `pubspec.lock`, the
package entry in `.dart_tool/package_config.json`, and the referenced materialization directory.
